    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0379" n="121" xml:id="pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1487</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-20T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 20, 1915, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 21, 2 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1656. My 1639, February 19, 10 p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d164-f1"/> Admiralty
                    desires further details about American steamers proceeding to England in order
                    safeguard their passage and asks for photographs, place of departure and
                    arrival, route, etc., also, if bound for Liverpool, information whether by north
                    or south of Ireland and approximate dates.</p>
                <p>Silhouette of American Line steamers <hi rendition="#italic">St. Paul</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic"> St. Louis, New York,</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philadelphia</hi> given to Admiralty and point of arrival and departure
                    stated to be Liverpool.</p>
                <p>I have no further information.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d164-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d164-f1" n="1" xml:id="d164-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d164-f2" n="2" xml:id="d164-f2-content">
                <p>By arrangement with the Department of Commerce, information as to the sailing of
                    American ships was thereafter regularly received and transmitted to the
                    Ambassador in Germany for communication to the Admiralty.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
